WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:10.420
Arguably, the primary source of all fear,
sorrow, and existential conflict is the self-awareness

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.940
and foresight of our mortality.

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:20.380
The fact that we can live a life that feels
so real, so important, and so incredible,

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:24.330
that we are compelled to want it to go on
forever.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:31.210
The fact that we can speculate and comprehend
the possibility of the infinite yet be forced

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:38.500
to live with the realization that we are finite,
and everything we do and care about is subject

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.980
to the short timeline of our life.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:47.780
At some point, everything will evaporate away
into nothingness.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.000
As humans, this is our curse.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:58.079
We are the seam between the infinite and the
finite, able to ponder and long for the eternal,

00:00:58.079 --> 00:01:03.920
yet be bound to the impermanence of our deteriorating
body.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:10.380
But perhaps in some strange puzzling way,
this is also our blessing.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:15.470
Currently, we cannot control the biology of
our human organism.

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:23.200
We cannot control the fact that we live inside
of a decomposing carbon-based body destine

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.550
for expiration.

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:32.049
But we can control, at least to some degree,
the way we view and think about things from

00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:33.580
within it.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:40.079
And so we can control how we think about the
idea of our death and rationalize with it

00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:46.350
in a way that reduces some of its torment
and allows us to make the best of our life

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.890
before it arrives.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:55.759
In order to do so, consider a video game,
board game, or sports game that you have played

00:01:55.759 --> 00:01:57.850
in the past.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:02.899
What was the driving force of playing said
game?

00:02:02.899 --> 00:02:08.750
Certainly you enjoyed playing the game for
itself, but you were ultimately playing towards

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.270
something.

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:14.280
You were playing the game towards an endpoint.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:21.050
And arguably, you only played the game because
you knew there would be an endpoint.

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:27.900
The human mind is seemingly fixed on requiring
an endpoint to derive meaning and motivation

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.920
for doing things.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.690
What would a game be without an end?

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.550
Would we even play?

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:38.950
What would a story be without a conclusion?

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:47.019
Everything we construct and do in life, whether
intentional or not, has an endpoint.

00:02:47.019 --> 00:02:48.580
Death is life’s endpoint.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:56.319
It is our motivation to play the game of life
and to create our narrative within it.

00:02:56.319 --> 00:03:03.080
Without it, we would not care to leave legacies
through our careers, passions, and families.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:07.879
We would not want to positively impact the
world around us.

00:03:07.879 --> 00:03:15.590
We would not be inspired to create fascinating
art, develop exciting technology, and incite

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:18.550
innovative ways of thinking.

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:24.409
And we would not work to make the best out
of life and find wonder in all its simple

00:03:24.409 --> 00:03:26.670
pleasures.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:32.659
To live with the knowledge and angst of our
impending mortality is undoubtedly the curse

00:03:32.659 --> 00:03:35.040
of humankind.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:40.409
But it is paradoxically our blessing in disguise.

00:03:40.409 --> 00:03:44.879
Perhaps our brains cannot discern meaningful
existence without an endpoint, and because

00:03:44.879 --> 00:03:47.340
our experience of life is subjective and transient,
we are able to find great value and meaningfulness

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:48.340
within it.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:52.030
Ironically, death is the reason why we cherish
life so deeply.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:58.110
And it is because we cherish life so deeply
that we fear death with such great intensity.

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:06.680
Together, life and death function in a feedback
loop, creating the highly unique and expressive

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:07.680
human experience of reality.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:12.030
This is not to suggest that we should be fearless
of death and look forward to its arrival.

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:16.409
I would be a liar if did not admit that I
too yearn to live on into eternity with full

00:04:16.409 --> 00:04:17.409
self-awareness.

00:04:17.409 --> 00:04:18.409
But as long as humans are still humans, forced
to live with the looming anticipation of an

00:04:18.409 --> 00:04:19.409
ever-approaching endpoint, I am merely suggesting
that we try our best to create and understand

00:04:19.409 --> 00:04:20.409
death’s practical purpose and value in life
itself.

00:04:20.409 --> 00:04:21.409
They say that it is not the destination that
counts, but the journey.

00:04:21.409 --> 00:04:22.409
And this is certainly true.

00:04:22.409 --> 00:04:24.400
But I would argue that a journey needs some
sort of destination for it to even be a journey

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:25.630
in the first place.

